 The global DRM rotation matrix (`sDrmGlRotation`, `NanoMenuDrm.h`) is uploaded to every
 shader once per frame (upload-on-change) so all geometry comes out panel-native.
 
+## Displays: one screen at a time
+
+Every screen is independent and draws at its own native mode; nothing is mirrored or scaled.
+Only one is on at a time. While a monitor (HDMI or DisplayPort) is plugged in, system_server
+makes it display 0 and switches the panel off (`LogicalDisplayMapper.gammaosArrangeLocked`, the
+decisions in `services/.../display/GammaosScreenArrangement.java`); unplugged, the panel is
+display 0 again. Apps, IME, dialogs and games follow display 0 by themselves.
+
+Nano draws on the display showing layer stack 0 (`NanoDisplayTarget.h`; `NanoDisplayTargetSf.h`
+reads SurfaceFlinger's displays, shared with drastic-nano). `followDisplay0()` runs every 500 ms
+from the frame loop: it moves Nano's layer and token to that display, and the home re-creates its
+surface at the display's mode (`resizeFlingerSurface`, shared with the overlay's rotation resize).
+A monitor's projection belongs to WindowManager, so Nano sets the projection only on a panel.
+While a monitor is the screen (`mTargetMonitor`) the touchscreen is ignored, no second-panel
+surfaces are made, and drastic-nano launches through SurfaceFlinger (the DRM backend can only
+drive the panel). There is no mirror of Nano's layer. Nano assumes no resolution: everything
+sizes from the active mode.
+
+system_server holds each monitor at one of its modes, so frame rate votes and apps can't move it
+(`GammaosScreenArrangement.monitorMode`): a running trial, else the mode stored for that monitor,
+else Auto (`autoMode`: 1080p nearest 60 Hz, the mode the kernel DisplayPort driver makes
+preferred, else the largest offered mode at 50-61 Hz). Stored modes are kept per monitor model (a
+hash of its product info, `monitorKey`) in `/data/system/gammaos_monitor_modes.txt`, with an
+applying marker while a stored mode is being set: a monitor that doesn't get through it runs at
+Auto at its next connect, and its stored mode is dropped. Nano's Settings > Display Settings >
+External Display (Output Resolution, Refresh Rate, Forget Monitor Resolutions; also in the Quick
+Menu; `NanoMenuMonitorMode.cpp`) picks modes through `cmd display gammaos-monitor-mode` (`try`
+runs a mode as a 15 s trial that system_server reverts unless Nano sends `keep`) and reads the
+mode held and why from `sys.gammaos.display.monitor_mode`. Which modes the driver offers is
+Thimsy's `scripts/sprd_drm.py`.
+
